# Database repositories

Each Supabase table has one file under `src/features/<feature>/db/`. CPQ uses `configuration.ts` for `cpq.configurations`. CRM customers stay in `src/features/crm/common/db/customer.ts` and the customers view reads that list. `src/features/crm/common/db/deal-customer.ts` is the repository for `crm.deal_customers`. Deals use `src/features/crm/deals/db/deal.ts`. `src/features/crm/deals/db/deal-quote.ts` is the repository for `crm.deal_quotes`. A deal keeps its first quote on `deals.quote_id` and can have more quotes through that table. There is no active quote. Conversations use `src/features/crm/conversations/db/conversation.ts`, `activity.ts`, and `call.ts`. A call activity points at `crm.calls` through `activities.call_id`. `activities.generated_by` is `ai` or `manual`. Quotes use `src/features/crm/quotes/db/quote.ts` against `crm.quotes`. `src/features/crm/quotes/db/quote-revision.ts` is the repository for `crm.quote_revisions`. A quote points at its active revision through `quotes.active_revision_id`. `quotes.status` and `quote_revisions.status` are `draft`, `sent`, `viewed`, `changes_requested`, `signed`, `deposit_paid`, `expired`, or `voided`. The full configuration lives on `crm.quote_revisions.config`. `crm.quote_revisions.config_changes` stores only the parameters that changed from the previous revision. `crm.quote_revisions.shared_photos_at` is when photos for that revision were attached, and `crm.quote_revisions.shared_quote_at` is when Review & Send shared that revision. Both are null until then. `crm.quote_revisions.renders` stores `render_full_url`, `render_medium_url`, and `render_small_url` for the perspective images in the public `quote-revision-renders` bucket. Review & Send communication lives on `crm.quote_revisions`. `crm.quotes` does not store the configuration. CPQ writes those rows through that repository. AI uses `yard-preview.ts` for `ai.yard_previews` and `suggestion.ts` for `ai.suggestions`. A suggestion stores the deal id, the inbound activity ids that produced it, an intent of `revision` or `new_quote`, a status of `pending`, `applied`, or `dismissed`, `config_changes` as JSON in the same shape as `crm.quote_revisions.config_changes`, and `preview_image_url` for the PNG in the public `ai-suggestions` bucket.

The quotes view does not add a second repository for `crm.quotes`.

The file exports CRUD only:

- `create…` inserts a row
- `read…` loads a row
- `update…` changes a row
- `delete…` removes a row

Validate write payloads with a Zod schema from `types/index.ts` before the query. Return the row or a typed record. Do not calculate prices, format text, or reshape data for the UI here. Do not query another feature's tables.

Do not put mapper functions in `db/`. Turning a database row into a typed record, or one schema into another, belongs in `utils/mappers.ts`. Call that function from the repository.

```ts
export async function readCustomer(id: string): Promise<Customer | undefined> {
  const { data, error } = await crm().from("customers").select("id, full_name, phone, email, opted_out").eq("id", id).maybeSingle();
  throwIfError(error);
  if (!data) return undefined;
  return toCustomer(data as CustomerRow);
}
```
